VoxelsEngine — @VOXELS_VERSION@
================================

Thank you for trying VoxelsEngine, a first-person block-based voxel sandbox game.

Controls
--------
  Move                 W A S D
  Look                 Mouse
  Jump                 Space
  Sprint               Left Shift
  Break Block          Left Click
  Place Block          Right Click
  Hotbar Slot          1-9 or Mouse Wheel
  Pause / Back         Escape
  Debug Overlay        F3
  Screenshot           F2
This card is also shown in-game on first launch and is reopenable from the pause menu
("Controls").

Running the game
-----------------
Double-click voxels_app(.exe) to launch. The game creates its own save/settings/log
directory on first run (see "Where your data lives" below) — no installer is required.

Where your data lives
----------------------
Saves, settings, logs, and screenshots are stored outside this folder, in your OS user-data
directory, so they survive reinstalling or moving this folder:

  Windows   %LOCALAPPDATA%\VoxelsEngine\
  Linux     $XDG_DATA_HOME/VoxelsEngine/  (usually ~/.local/share/VoxelsEngine/)
  macOS     ~/Library/Application Support/VoxelsEngine/

Reporting a bug
----------------
Each session writes a timestamped log file to the "logs" folder under the path above
(e.g. VoxelsEngine\logs\voxels_<timestamp>.log on Windows). Please attach that file, along
with a description of what you were doing, to your bug report.

System requirements
--------------------
  OS:        Windows 10/11, a modern Linux desktop, or macOS 11+
  GPU:       Any GPU with OpenGL 3.3 Core support and up-to-date vendor drivers
  Storage:   ~200 MB
  Input:     Keyboard and mouse

Known limitations (this build)
-------------------------------
  * World generation, lighting propagation across chunk boundaries, and multiplayer
    prediction/reconciliation are still being refined — see ARCHITECTURE.md in the source
    repository for the honest, current subsystem status.
  * Most in-game textures, sounds, and models are procedurally generated placeholder content,
    not final hand-authored art; see ASSET_REQUESTS.md in the source repository.
  * Steam integration (achievements, overlay, cloud saves), when present in this build, requires
    the Steam client to be running; the game plays identically without it.

Version
-------
VoxelsEngine v@VOXELS_VERSION@
